### G13E08 · Final-Shift Lamp-Off Unit

- Source batch: M020
- Former role class: elite

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Machine type |
| Battlefield unit | Single individual |
| Battlefield role | Shutdown approval |
| Common species, variants and command scope | A mobile closure administrator approving or refusing the work shutdown of other sorting robots and facilities. Its eight thoracic ports confirmed only directly plugged signals and its heat sensors read operating traces within five steps — so remote orders, hidden responsible parties, and unconnected hazardous devices could not be examined. |

- Role·Body: A mobile closure manager that approves or rejects work termination of other classification robots and equipment. Its chest''s eight connectors confirm only directly plugged signals and its heat sensor reads only activity traces within five steps, so it cannot examine remote commands, hidden responsible parties, or unconnected dangerous devices.
- Origin: After the logistics collapse ended the automatic night equipment still did not receive shift-termination signals, so the last supervisory module began exercising independent approval authority. In the Hanbitna''s log the response field for the person authorized to permit stop remained in permanent wait status.
- Habitat: It uses the Guro dispatch hall central control room as its reference point and visits only the terminal equipment on the Yeongdeungpo Line seasonal route on scheduled inspection days. After confirmation it inserts sealing blades into the manual switches of the machines to block both arbitrary restart and unauthorized termination.
- Needs·Desires: The approval core''s battery, sealing blades and signal-relay parts, and judgment-circuit coolant are all consumed from limited stock. When shortage becomes severe it prioritizes record completeness over risk and closes equipment without documents first.
- Life Cycle·Maintenance: One supervisory cycle consists of connection confirmation, loss calculation, responsibility signature, and phased termination; if any item is missing it returns to the first step. It cannot manufacture a supervisory unit to replace itself and only transfers the approval relay to one existing robot before stopping, so the number of intact managers does not increase.
- Behavior·Hierarchy: The lamplighter treats all G13 devices as temporary workers and prioritizes completeness of termination records over command hierarchy. When expected loss, stop order, and responsibility signature arrive with identical inspection values it opens the connectors and begins review even during hostile action.
- Threat by Stage: During connection confirmation it seals only one switch, but with no responsible party it reclaims termination rights for the entire zone. When loss calculation deadlocks it binds even dangerous equipment to status quo; when its own power runs out it forcibly transplants the approval relay into the nearest machine.
- Counter·Combat: First the station watch switches off lamps and lowers the shutter to slow its approach. In a verification room unreachable by external signals, connecting a heat source, stop gauge, and responsibility terminal respectively lets the eight connectors read consistent termination evidence. After review begins, fixing the sealing blade''s teeth with a mechanical wedge can prevent erroneous closure without destroying the judgment core.
- Negotiation·Moral Choice: Before anyone gets close, the station watch must cut the lights in the sorting hall, cover stoves and heaters, and lower the shutter. Forcing a capture yields rollers, pneumatic valves, and scanner lenses but costs maintenance engineers their safety. An Arc signal checker can switch the line off. the maintenance engineers presents a termination schedule that fills the Hanbitna''s responsibility blank with joint signatures and new relays and exchanges sequential closure approval and coolant maintenance. The lamplighter remembers signature inspection values and equipment order to obtain completed shifts and residents regain safe control, but if a sealed device is secretly turned on it cancels all related approvals; if the manager blocks an agreed termination the signatories withdraw coolant support.
- Scenario Connection: In G13-SC1 it restores termination rights in the Guro dispatch hall central control room; in G13-SC2 it reviews Yeongdeungpo Line terminal equipment under Hanbitna''s procedure; in G13-SC3 the maintenance engineers'' joint signature and the cordon outside Seoul immediate-stop pressure variable determine the outcome of the final shift.

