<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0140"></a>

### Role and Body

A trade specialist carrying a nutrient-pack pump and sickbed number plates, delivering along the rail.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0142"></a>

### Origin

After the ration timetable and the sickbed prescription table merged, even cancelled supplies kept being carried out.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0144"></a>

### Habitat and Needs

It circles the nutrient-pump station and the sickbed rail, needing packs, tubes, cleaning fluid, and charging.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0146"></a>

### Life and Maintenance

When a tube clogs it marks that sickbed as starving and locks the door until cleaning ends.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0148"></a>

### Behavior and Hierarchy

As the head of the pump band it follows the rounds car''s roster and supplies no one without a number.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0150"></a>

### Escalation

Stage 1 delays supply, stage 2 reclaims packs, and stage 3 locks the whole sickbed zone''s rations.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0152"></a>

### Engagement and Response

Connecting a manual flow table and a cleaning loop releases it, and destroying the pump costs food.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0154"></a>

### Negotiation and Moral Choice

Handing filter and pump parts to the maintenance engineers lets the station watch borrow this unit''s work one shift at a time. This type does not become a unit, so capture only yields parts. Accurate rationing can be entrusted to it, but a reserve share for people off the roster must be publicly set aside.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0156"></a>

### Scenario Links

G15-SC2, G15-SC3.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G15-heading-0158"></a>
<a id="g15e08"></a>

### G15E08 · White-Strap Restraint Unit

- Source batch: M024
- Former role class: first elite

| Bestiary item | Record |
