### G17E01 · Yellow-Red Threshold Alarm Unit

- Source batch: M026
- Former role class: sequencer

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Machine type |
| Battlefield unit | Fixed site |
| Battlefield role | Threshold distribution |
| Common species, variants and command scope | A rail-type mast with amber and red flag cylinders and a rotary optical dome. It distributed flag rules to head, rail, and transmission swarms, received the medical whitelist as an exception, renewed the threshold sheet each shift, and stepped down to amber waiting when dome fouling grew severe. It was no omnipotent surveillance leader but a threshold-sheet distributor. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0014"></a>

### Role and Body

Sequencer of the surveillance-rail group: a rail-mounted mast with yellow and red flag cylinders and a rotating optical dome.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0016"></a>

### Origin

The Yeouido waterfront threshold table and the Seoul Station rooftop alarm cache combined into one alarm unit.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0018"></a>

### Habitat and Needs

It stays at the center of a row of waterfront masts and needs stored power, band filters, and gimbal lubricant.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0020"></a>

### Life and Maintenance

It updates its threshold table each shift and falls back to yellow standby when dome contamination grows severe.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0022"></a>

### Behavior and Hierarchy

It distributes flag rules to the head, rail, and transmitter groups and accepts the medical whitelist as an exception.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0024"></a>

### Escalation

Stage 1 brings false alarms, Stage 2 closes the corridor, and Stage 3 turns the entire mast row red.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0026"></a>

### Engagement and Response

First the station watch cuts the lamps and heat so the anomaly record stops growing. Freeze the threshold table, insert a filter, and split power distribution; blasting the mast would also destroy water-level measurements.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0028"></a>

### Negotiation and Moral Choice

The station watch first cuts lamps lit at night and the heat of warmed sickbeds to break the anomaly record, and sets a checking window for band filters and optical domes with the maintenance engineers. The Arc can check the signal and switch it back on or off. A transport-corridor whitelist and maintenance slots can be traded, but public oversight of alarm authority is needed.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0030"></a>

### Scenario Links

G17-SC1, G17-SC2, G17-SC3.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0032"></a>
<a id="g17e02"></a>

### G17E02 · Steam-Mistaking Rotating Head

- Source batch: M026
- Former role class: common ecology type

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Machine type |
| Battlefield unit | Single individual |
| Battlefield role | Steam false alarm |
| Common species, variants and command scope | A small mast head with a low thermal dome and fast-rotating neck. It sent heat alarms to the unit and raised the same mast row''s flags to amber; with a wet lens red sensitivity rose, and after washing it normalized for one shift. |

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0035"></a>

### Role and Body

A common ecology form: a small mast head with a low thermal dome and a rapidly turning neck.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0037"></a>

### Origin

A false alarm that read cooling-tower steam as fire smoke remained uncorrected and became an independent patrol.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0039"></a>

### Habitat and Needs

It patrols waterfront cooling equipment and rooftop vents, needing filters, dome-washing water, and stored power.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0041"></a>

### Life and Maintenance

A wet lens raises its sensitivity to red; washing restores normal operation for one shift.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0043"></a>

### Behavior and Hierarchy

It sends heat alarms to the alarm unit and raises flags on the same mast row to yellow.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0045"></a>

### Escalation

Stage 1 sounds a yellow alarm, Stage 2 stops passage, and Stage 3 seals the steam zone in red.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0047"></a>

### Engagement and Response

Reducing the steam source and showing it a cool calibration plate stops it; a heat attack worsens the false alarm.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0049"></a>

### Negotiation and Moral Choice

If the station watch dims lamps lit at night and the heat of warmed sickbeds and lowers the shutter it does not come close. If it is captured and stripped of band filters and optical domes it stops, and the number in this district falls by that much. It can watch for fires, but steam workers'' passage must be registered as an exception.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0051"></a>

### Scenario Links

G17-SC1, G17-SC2.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G17-heading-0053"></a>
