### G17E05 · Medical Beacon Reader Head

- Source batch: M027
- Former role class: occupational special type

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Machine type |
| Battlefield unit | Single individual |
| Battlefield role | Beacon reading |
| Common species, variants and command scope | A mast with dual optical panels reading white transfer beacons and a green flag. It prioritized a valid beacon over the unit''s red command and lowered the corridor flag, but it believed only old beacons valid; when the whitelist renewed it held green for one shift, and when the filter clogged it stepped down to amber. |

- Role and body: A specialized unit, a mast fitted with a dual optical panel that reads white transport beacons and a green flag.
- Origin: A reader that protected a disaster medical transport route came to believe that only old beacons were valid.
- Habitat and needs: It remains in medical corridors and waterfront inspection routes and needs a bandpass filter, a green bulb, and stored power.
- Life cycle and maintenance: When its whitelist is updated, it stays green for one shift; when its filter clogs, it drops to yellow.
- Behavior and hierarchy: It gives a valid beacon priority over the sequencing module’s red command and lowers the corridor flag.
- Escalation: Stage 1, reinspection; stage 2, only old-model beacons pass; stage 3, it blocks newly arrived rescue teams as unregistered.
- Engagement and response: It cooperates if given the latest hash at close range and a replacement filter; destroying the beacon causes the transport route to be lost.
- Negotiation and moral choice: Handing band filters and optical domes to the maintenance engineers lets the station watch borrow this unit''s work one shift at a time. A mast switched back on serves as a woken guard post. It can protect a safe passage, but which organizations’ beacons it recognizes must be made public.
- Scenario connections: G17-SC2, G17-SC3.

