### G25E07 · Gap-Leaping Grasshopper

- Source batch: M040
- Former role class: mobile special type

| Bestiary item | Record |
|---|---|
| Type | Machine type |
| Battlefield unit | Single individual |
| Battlefield role | Maneuver · flank |
| Common species, variants and command scope | The Gap-Crossing Grasshopper was a machine chassis type differentiated from the G25 common ecology. The maneuver · flank role applied only at the independent-unit scope, and stood in for neither the whole swarm''s ecological order nor human command. |

- Role and body: A grasshopper-shaped messenger with jumping springs concealed in its dish-shaped hind knees. It can cross short gaps but cannot freely change direction in midair.
- Origin: A pre-Blackout launcher aid that sent the leading end of a rescue rope between broken stairways restarted in the Yongsan Line drop-test room. The landing-approval plate is at an old coordinate.
- Habitat and needs: It stays near short breaks in Mapo gallery floor. Without spring lubricant and landing cushioning, wear limits its trips before its charge does.
- Life cycle and maintenance: It measures the difference in elasticity between its two hind legs on a docking scale. If one weakens, it stops jumping and climbs down the wall; it cannot make a new spring.
- Behavior and hierarchy: The line must be pulled at the arrival point before it calls the next messenger. It sometimes reads a reflective fragment of a demolished platform as an intact landing pad.
- Escalation: At stage 1, it leaps into empty space; at stage 2, it winds rescue rope around railings. When stage 3 units gather awaiting launch, there is no room to move on either side of the staircase.
- Combat and response: Move the landing plate to a nearby safe support so the spring releases without a load. Shooting it in midair can make the attached rope drag evacuees.
- Negotiation and moral choice: In exchange for handing storage cells, precision motors, and optical lenses to the maintenance engineers, the station watch borrows this machine''s work one shift at a time. A captured and repaired swarm becomes a search-light drone swarm. Require a person to confirm the landing for every jump. Faster communication comes at the cost of keeping someone on duty on both sides of the staircase.
- Scenario connections: G25-SC1, G25-SC2, G25-SC3.

